<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:09:40Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>German state elections deal a blow to Chancellor Friedrich Merz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:289145345278a095da2a455542ceaa57b06cb9eae25d98eb2906aac1743e7bac</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:09:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T21:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-state-elections-deal-a-blow-to-chancellor-friedrich-merz/a-79348585--45dd8fc79779.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-state-elections-deal-a-blow-to-chancellor-friedrich-merz/a-79348585?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Elections in Berlin and Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania have dealt the CDU a historic defeat while the AfD saw a massive gain. The pressure on Germany's unpopular chancellor is mounting.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>AfD makes gains in state elections, but has no government options</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a8bf8b5ba7560adefea3e9e5888f47348daadf40f1bbdbf25f2fdb207ddad64f</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:09:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T19:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/afd-makes-gains-in-state-elections-but-has-no-government-options/a-79348308--1a6e760f93a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afd-makes-gains-in-state-elections-but-has-no-government-options/a-79348308?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite making significant gains in both Berlin and Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania, the far-right AfD remains without options to form a state government.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Doctors offer Oktoberfest flu jabs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0be2dade65a62bb2b3f01ab6ee08daa4179b741e4ef721dd5da10b33116311b8</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T06:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-doctors-offer-oktoberfest-flu-jabs/live-79335548--b4ec07a0d158.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-doctors-offer-oktoberfest-flu-jabs/live-79335548?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Oktoberfest 2026 is underway but it's not just beer on offer in Munich this year; revelers can also get themselves a flu jab before heading to the tents. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Oktoberfest opens as Munich mayor taps first beer keg</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e6d0ff9f8274dfdddf9f618fcbaf017aa9b05ec83649ce4689f111b3ec0da2d8</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T08:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/oktoberfest-opens-as-munich-mayor-taps-first-beer-keg/a-79336519--c14aa7f149ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/oktoberfest-opens-as-munich-mayor-taps-first-beer-keg/a-79336519?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Thousands of visitors streamed onto Munich's Oktoberfest grounds as the world-famous beer festival got underway. Some spent the night outside the gates to secure coveted places in the festival tents.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany faces energy tax losses as EV sales rise</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e8ef5fd77c14825522123bc7bfd3447fe3fe02fef8e1c899998c15402f71f9d5</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T14:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-faces-energy-tax-losses-as-ev-sales-rise/a-79320422--82b05ee44dbb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-faces-energy-tax-losses-as-ev-sales-rise/a-79320422?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The rapid shift to electric vehicles in Germany is cutting fuel tax revenue for the government. As EV sales surge, policymakers face growing pressure to find new ways to fund roads and transportation infrastructure.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Oktoberfest 2026: Everything you need to know</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3cbccf9af32cdf63c9de6475900a5f472f85406f291fd41048d07be45ce9b4c0</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T09:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/oktoberfest-2026-everything-you-need-to-know/a-79311285--1e3ee9d16248.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/oktoberfest-2026-everything-you-need-to-know/a-79311285?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">This year, AI will be used to manage overcrowded situations. Find all the numbers surrounding the fest — including the price of water!</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Saint, sinner or feminist icon: How Mary Magdalene's image evolved through time</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:10475d99568ef46e6b05f329349b3794a26cad58625799bdf37d419860531e14</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:33Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T07:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saint-sinner-or-feminist-icon-how-mary-magdalene-s-image-evolved-through-time/a-79293868--1a6f3ade345e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saint-sinner-or-feminist-icon-how-mary-magdalene-s-image-evolved-through-time/a-79293868?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From "Apostle of the Apostles" to prostitute, Mary Magdalene has been